>> title: Peanut, Black-Eyed Pea and Chicken Feet Soup
>> category: Soups
>> tags: chicken feet, pork, peanuts, black-eyed peas, cantonese, old-fire soup, spring, stovetop
>> counters: The Soup Pot
>> aka: 花生眉豆雞腳湯, faa sang mei dau gai goek tong, fa sang mei dau gai gerk tong, peanut black-eyed pea and chicken feet soup, chicken feet soup, 老火湯, lo fo tong
>> servings: 6
>> time: 3 hr 45 min
>> slack: forgiving — letting it reach a boil shakes the skin off the feet and into the broth, and the pot is cloudy from then on
>> step.1: The spring pot — 健脾祛濕 for the damp months. The feet are the body here and not the dish.
>> step.2: trim the nails, then blanch from cold
>> step.3: rinse the peanuts and the peas
>> step.4: simmer 3 hr, barely a quiver
>> step.5: season at the end, never at the start
>> step.6: The broth is the dish. The solids are spent.

The spring pot — 健脾祛濕, the damp months — and the clearest example on this shelf of a soup organised entirely by what its parts are for.

Trim the nails off @chicken feet{1%lb}(450 g), then blanch them from cold with @pork shin{3/4%lb}(340 g; in two pieces) in @water{2%qt}(1.9 L) in a #soup pot{}, ~blanch{10%min}. Pour it all away, rinse both and scrub the pot.

Rinse @raw peanuts{3/4%cup}(faa sang; raw, skins on, and they go in dry), @black-eyed peas{1/2%cup}(mei dau; 祛濕健脾 — the pair with the peanuts is what makes this a spring pot) and @red dates{4}(hung zou; pitted — the stone is held to make a pot 燥) under cold water.

Simmer @&(~2)blanched feet and shin{} with @&(~1)peanuts and peas{}, @ginger{3%slices} and @cold water{3%qt}(2.8 L; the pot is filled once and not topped up) in the rinsed #soup pot{}, lid ajar, ~simmer{3%hr} at a bare quiver, unstirred.

Season @&(~1)soup{} with @kosher salt{1%tsp}, at the end and never at the start.

The broth is the dish.
